      "writtenOn": "2024-08-28T00:59:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The partner can response with Wait. I can\u0027t recall seeing this happen in real life. Benson Leung might have. UCSI is silent on the PPM\u0027s reaction to a Wait. It\u0027s plausible that the PDC could wait (min 100 ms) and try again before this command times out.\n\nI actually did see \"WAIT\" as a response to some swaps at the USB-IF Compliance event 3 weeks back, but not a Data Role Swap. My traces show I captured a Wait after a PR_Swap.\n\nMost of the cases I captured of interop with other DRPs at the USB-IF compliance event where swaps were sent to us or from us were basically when we connect two laptops together. PDCs from TI and Cypress, representing a laptop formfactor, basically we were plugged into a similar design as our laptop.\n\nThe general consensus I saw at the event for this use case (two DRP/DRD devices that prefer to be DFP) was that whichever DRP/DRD comes up as UFP tries to send a DR_Swap, but the other partner sends a Reject, because it\u0027s happy with the DFP role.",
      "parentUuid": "98600789_d9339313",
